---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="About">
  <div class="container page">
    <article class="prose">
      <header class="page-head">
        <span class="section-eyebrow">About</span>
        <h1>About</h1>
      </header>

      <img class="portrait" src="/images/profile/oishee-rahman.jpg" alt="Oishee Rahman" width="400" height="400" />

      <h2>Professional Profile</h2>
      <p>
        Oishee Rahman is an energy policy researcher based in Dhaka, working on the regulation and institutions behind Bangladesh’s renewable energy transition. Her focus areas are agrivoltaics, grid and land-use policy, and making the energy transition inclusive of women and underserved communities.
      </p>
      <p>
        At GIZ Bangladesh’s Green Energy Transition–Policy Advisory Partnership (GET-PAP), she worked alongside the Power Division, SREDA and the EU Delegation. She coordinated the four sub-groups of the National Working Group on Agrivoltaics and Floating Solar, supported national consultations on solar O&amp;M standards and the draft onshore wind guideline, and analysed the regulatory framework for agrivoltaics adoption. That analysis later helped her in the research “Regulatory Barriers to Agrivoltaics Adoption in Bangladesh: A Policy Gap Analysis”, which she presented at the AgriVoltaics World Conference 2026.
      </p>
      <p>
        She is currently a member of the Just Energy Transition Advocacy Working Group at Manusher Jonno Foundation, developing policy recommendations on women’s participation in the energy transition. She is also an alumna of the Shoktikonna Leadership Cohort, a selective women’s leadership programme on Bangladesh’s green energy transition.
      </p>
      <p>
        Her technical grounding comes from a BSc and MS in Applied Chemistry and Chemical Engineering at the University of Dhaka. This included research on biodegradable polymer films and nanomaterials for wastewater treatment, which gives her policy work a solid understanding of the technologies it regulates.
      </p>
      <p>
        She is interested in policy advisory, research and programme roles that move Bangladesh’s renewable energy targets from paper to practice.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>

